From 5743431acd028470b403db9583bb4e36068b1237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:21:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(claims): T10 HTTP M1-M7/B1-B2, Studio Claims UI, buyer
 claim page, KC16
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements contracts/live-keyword-claims-v1.md §7 and §11.1 (T10b, unblocked by the
§0.1 ruling) on top of the T10 core (2e1f53d), MOCK/manual ingress only.

HTTP (§7):
- internal/httpapi/claims.go: M1-M7 under live-sessions/{session}/claims, mounted
  next to Studio only when Options.ClaimLabels is set; Studio private boundary
  (private no-store, query rejection except M6 limit/cursor, methodless 405),
  strict bodies with required keys and no top-level null (M4 "active" can never
  default to false), Idempotency-Key forbidden on reads / required on writes, 40P01
  and unknown errors -> 503. M7 writes the token only after WithScope returns nil
  (COMMIT), token null + replayed on replay, Referrer-Policy: no-referrer on every
  M7 answer. studio.go exposes studioDecodeRaw; handler.go adds scopedAs.
- internal/buyerhttp/claims.go: B1 GET claim-link / B2 POST claim-link/redeem with
  X-Commerce-Claim-Token exactly once (canonical, else 422), 403 for that header on
  any other route (forbiddenInput), explicit frozen projections, private no-store;
  PUT /v1/buyer/cart rejects Idempotency-Key "clm:*" with 422 (§5.6).
- cmd/api/claims.go: COMMERCE_CLAIMS_ENABLED (default off, requires Studio) and
  COMMERCE_CLAIMS_LABEL_KEY (canonical 32-byte key, distinct from every configured
  secret and key ring); the API refuses to start otherwise.

UI (§11.1):
- admin /{locale}/studio/claims (StudioClaims.tsx, claims.css; Studio link): window
  badge + Open/Close, rule selector while CLOSED, offers table/form (product -> SKU),
  per-reason counters with "pin the host prompt", frozen host prompts (zh-TW/zh-CN/en
  verbatim), MOCK manual entry, buyers/links table, masked one-time link dialog
  (reveal/copy/discard). BFF allowlist exactly M1-M7 (claims-request.ts, proxy.ts).
- storefront /{locale}/claim (ClaimLink.tsx): #t= read then replaceState, token in
  memory only, no-referrer header + meta, preview with price/stock notes, explicit
  add (one key per click), contract 404/409 copy, cart review; BFF allowlist B1/B2
  forwarding the token header only there (buyer-server.ts, buyer-client.ts).
- Composition recorded for owner review in .impeccable/live-claims-brief.md.

Tests: httpapi/buyerhttp/cmd/api unit tests; node tests for the admin claims grammar,
frozen copy and the storefront claim BFF; KC16 TestBrowserLiveClaimsRealChain +
tests/admin/claims-ui.spec.ts via test-local.sh --browser-live-claims (admin +
storefront production Next, Go, PG18, signed MOCK IdP, local buyer.example TLS edge).

NOT_RUN: KC13/KC14 real-PG HTTP gates (test_worker), core-openapi.json M1-M7 and
tasks.json amendment (integrator; check_packet pins 8 operations), full foundation
suite, owner visual review.

